title: Aegis APPROVE F2–F6, with M1 (silent join of the device unlock) and M2 (an off-ruling reconsider tuple); the grant can be one prompt
summary: |-
  Verified: a standing grant only replaces the presence prompt inside the human-only approve. Root, hand-only, CLI, withdraw, peer and irreversible cards are excluded, and tuples come from kernel-written raise detail. The device id is kernel-bound from launch or resume and can't be forged by a page or session; sessions can't read device keys. Standing decisions still carry approvals-key signatures that replay verifies. Grants end on session end and helper exit, and the stores fold kernel-signed rows only. The F3 home check is realpath and case-folded.
  M1: a new GUI connection (e.g. via a stolen CLI key or a resume token) silently rides the 12 h device unlock, so log an approval.unlock.joined row and show it in the feed. M2: reconsider:extend crept in beyond the ruling; remove it and require a repo.
  L1: the presence row on mode loosen is wrong. L2: a test-only software-sig path. L3: the restart tuple must hash binaries kernel-side. L4: the grant fold survives a restart but is safe on the helper path.
  The two-prompt grant was unnecessary: make only the standing-grant card fresh class (one password). All of this was sent back to the builder with a merge of feat/gnomon.
symbols_touched:
